  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Warm the oil in the soup pot over medium heat. Cook the onion and carrots with a pinch of the salt for 8 minutes, until the onion is translucent and the carrot has softened.",
      "timer_min": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the garlic and cook for 1 minute.",
      "timer_min": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the tomato paste, cumin, and paprika and fry for 1 minute, stirring constantly or the paste will scorch - it is done when it brickens and smells sweet.",
      "timer_min": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the lentils, crushed tomatoes, and 5 cups of water. Bring to a boil, then lower to a bare simmer and cook for 20 minutes, until the lentils collapse and the carrot crushes against the pot side.",
      "timer_min": 20
    },
    {
      "text": "Blend the soup until velvety with the immersion blender, or leave half of it unblended if you want texture. It should pour like heavy cream; whisk in hot water to loosen if it has gone thick."
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir in the lemon juice and the dried mint - mint blooms in the hot soup, so let it sit for a minute before tasting. Season with the remaining salt and the black pepper; the soup should taste lemony first, with mint arriving late."
    },
    {
      "text": "Ladle into bowls and float the parsley and a pinch of chili flakes over each. Offer extra lemon wedges at the table."
    }
  ],
